things:
The songsters twittered in the rustling trees.
And all things were transfigured in the day,
But me whom radiant beauty could not move;

third:
I saw his soul saw,—‘Jasper first,’ I said,
‘And second, sapphire; third, chalcedony;
The rest in order, ... last, an amethyst.’

thin:
Where still their rotted stalks were to be seen;
The thin log snapped; and she went out for wood,
Bareheaded, running the few steps between

thinned:
The bright drops ring like bells of glass
Thinned by the wind, and lightly blown;
Sleep cannot fall on peaceful grass

thing's:
And ape a Bourbon in a crown of straws;
The thing’s too common.
Many fervent souls

thicket:
Pity me not for beauties passed away
From field and thicket as the year goes by;
Pity me not the waning of the moon,

thirsted:
A coronet to find;
Who never thirsted, flagons
And cooling tamarind.

thinkin:
An' all his children lef' to home a diggin' an' a-workin'.
A widower he was, an' Sal was thinkin' 'at she 'd wing him;
I reckon he was wond'rin' what them rings o' hern would bring him.

thins:
Break lashing me through hours of soulful dread;
But when the terror thins and, spent, withdraws,
Leaving me wondering awhile, I pause--

thickset:
My heart is like an apple-tree
Whose boughs are bent with thickset fruit;
My heart is like a rainbow shell

things'll:
But I tell you, fellah christuns,
Things'll happen mighty strange;
Now, de Lawd done dis fu' Isrul,

thirsting:
'T is beggars banquets best define;
'T is thirsting vitalizes wine, --
Faith faints to understand.

Where souls brimfull of love abide and meet;
Where thirsting longing eyes
Watch the slow door
